Open a file through the legacy extern FIFO (the no-plumber "B" file-open path):
the terminal reads the FIFO via extproc, feeds it as keyboard input, and types
the request into the command window, exactly as a plumbed showfile would.

-- input --
extern B sample.txt\n
-- waitframes --
28 49
-- drawops --
JIqbbAbddbbbbdbbbbdbbbYbilbbd{5}bbd{46}l{11}dddxdd
